From 3848fbcd1bbde6939c5c17e17390ce76c6f73b8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 12:33:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] De-card the runs/[id] route, promote client switching, split
 RM findings by skill
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

De-carding (runs/[id] page + every skill view):
- Added the dashboard's hyper-micro dot-grid background to
  runs/[id]/page.tsx, replacing the page's opaque background.
- Stripped surface-glass/border/bg "card" wrappers from every section on
  the run detail page (Step-by-step log, Summary, Details, deliverables
  loading/empty states) and across all 12 skill-specific view files
  (pin-down, pile-on, pre-call-read, win-back, leak-map, rep-onboarding,
  rep-engine-panel, rep-trustpilot/reddit/twitter-watch,
  rep-crisis-response) plus the shared run-activity-panel/empty-state/
  view-switcher/adhoc-run-summary-view components. Kept header/divider
  rows, row-level divide-y lists, form-input borders, and semantic
  colored alerts (severity/incident/failure banners) — only removed the
  generic card chrome around otherwise-neutral panels.

Client switching:
- Promoted workspace switching (each workspace is one client) from a
  generic "Workspaces" list buried in the avatar's account-settings
  popover to a labeled "Clients" button on the primary rail, with search
  for accounts with many clients.
- /api/workspaces/[id]/switch now redirects straight to that client's
  engagement profile instead of generic Work/home.

Reputation Manager findings:
- The 4 RM "watch" workers (engine panel, Trustpilot, Reddit, Twitter)
  now each get their own bookmarkable link into the shared findings
  page via a `?source=` filter, instead of all landing on the
  unfiltered mixed feed.
- rep-crisis-response now routes to the existing incident-lifecycle
  tracker (dashboard/reputation-manager/incidents — resolve, choose
  posture, escalate) instead of the read-only findings feed, since
  managing an incident and browsing a findings stream are genuinely
  different jobs. Incidents still appear in the mixed timeline
  read-only for cross-source context.
- Replaced workers-panel.tsx's duplicate inline href-building logic
  with the canonical workerPrimaryHref() from worker-registry.ts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
